From 502fd1b1279547f12775d84b279ff69a9e2bcc71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:17:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 105/210] drm/meson: encoder_hdmi: offer 10-bit deep color on
 GXM

GXM has a 10-bit video pipeline that dithers 12 bits down to 10, and
HDMI PLL settings for the deep color VCOs. GXBB and GXL convert 8 bits
to 10 in front of the HDMI controller, so a deeper wire format there
carries upconverted data at a higher clock and gains nothing.

Offer 10-bit deep color on GXM and keep 12 bits for the G12A family.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c
index 599e64c1311d..f383df2b067e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c
@@ -355,6 +355,11 @@ meson_encoder_hdmi_get_inp_bus_fmts(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 		return NULL;
 
 	if (meson_encoder_hdmi_fmt_depth(output_fmt) > 8 &&
+	    !meson_vpu_is_compatible(encoder_hdmi->priv, VPU_COMPATIBLE_G12A) &&
+	    !meson_vpu_is_compatible(encoder_hdmi->priv, VPU_COMPATIBLE_GXM))
+		return NULL;
+
+	if (meson_encoder_hdmi_fmt_depth(output_fmt) > 10 &&
 	    !meson_vpu_is_compatible(encoder_hdmi->priv, VPU_COMPATIBLE_G12A))
 		return NULL;
 
